{"name":"Decadence","hex":"#73667b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"decadence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["With a negative connotation: the process of declining from a state of moral virtue, prosperity, etc., to a worse state; decay, deterioration; also, the bad state which has been reached;  an instance of this.","An age or period of time when art, literature, etc., is regarded as having declined."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decadence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Decadence","blocks":[{"text":"Decadence was a late-19th-century movement emphasizing the need for sensationalism, egocentricity, and bizarre, artificial, perverse, and exotic sensations and experiences. By extension, it may refer to a decline in art, literature, science, technology, and work ethics, or to self-indulgent behavior."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Henryk_Siemiradzki_004.jpeg/330px-Henryk_Siemiradzki_004.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decadence"},{"title":"Decadence (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Decadence is the debut studio album of American rock band Head Automatica that was released on August 17, 2004, through Warner Bros. Records. Vocalist Daryl Palumbo toured as a member of Glassjaw until early 2003, when he wrote material for a new band. Shortly afterwards, he formed Head Automatica with drummer Larry Gorman and producer Dan \"Dan the Automator\" Nakamura. Recording sessions for their debut were held in September and October 2003 at The Glue Factory in San Francisco, California, with Nakamura producing the majority of the songs and Howard Benson producing two of them. Decadence is a dance-rock, garage rock, and electronic rock album that was influenced by the works of Joe Jackson, Nick Lowe, and Primal Scream."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/DecadenceHeadAutomatica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decadence_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/THOMAS_COUTURE_-_Los_Romanos_de_la_Decadencia_%28Museo_de_Orsay%2C_1847._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo%2C_472_x_772_cm%29.jpg/500px-THOMAS_COUTURE_-_Los_Romanos_de_la_Decadencia_%28Museo_de_Orsay%2C_1847._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo%2C_472_x_772_cm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/THOMAS_COUTURE_-_Los_Romanos_de_la_Decadencia_%28Museo_de_Orsay%2C_1847._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo%2C_472_x_772_cm%29.jpg/1280px-THOMAS_COUTURE_-_Los_Romanos_de_la_Decadencia_%28Museo_de_Orsay%2C_1847._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo%2C_472_x_772_cm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/THOMAS_COUTURE_-_Los_Romanos_de_la_Decadencia_%28Museo_de_Orsay%2C_1847._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo%2C_472_x_772_cm%29.jpg/500px-THOMAS_COUTURE_-_Los_Romanos_de_la_Decadencia_%28Museo_de_Orsay%2C_1847._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo%2C_472_x_772_cm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Romans during the Decadence, by Thomas Couture","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATHOMAS_COUTURE_-_Los_Romanos_de_la_Decadencia_(Museo_de_Orsay%2C_1847._%C3%93leo_sobre_lienzo%2C_472_x_772_cm).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heliogabalus_High_Priest_of_the_Sun.jpg/250px-Heliogabalus_High_Priest_of_the_Sun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Heliogabalus_High_Priest_of_the_Sun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heliogabalus_High_Priest_of_the_Sun.jpg/250px-Hel